# Postgres connection-pool ceilings per process (assessment 5-3).
#
#   backend <n>   KNEX_POOL_MAX on the backend Container App (× up to 3
#                 replicas, each with its own pool)
#   worker <n>    KNEX_POOL_MAX on the jobs-worker Container App
#
# The arithmetic this bounds: B_Standard_B1ms allows ~35 connections. The
# old default of 10 per process × 3 backend replicas + the worker + a
# migration run ≈ 40 — over budget, and the 30 s acquire timeout turned
# that into 30-second hangs. 6 × 3 + 8 + 1 = 27 leaves headroom for a
# migration and a psql session. Raise the SKU before raising these.
#
# Editing this file on main runs .github/workflows/db-pool.yml, which sets
# KNEX_POOL_MAX on both apps (a new backend revision at 0% traffic, then
# health-checked and shifted; the worker simply restarts). No-op when the
# values already match — NOT a promote vehicle. infra/variables.tf carries
# the same defaults (backend_pool_max / jobs_worker_pool_max) so a later
# terraform apply agrees.
#
